.TH SDL_NULL_WHILE_LOOP_CONDITION 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_NULL_WHILE_LOOP_CONDITION \- A macro for wrapping code in
.BR "do {} while (0);"
without compiler warnings.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_NULL_WHILE_LOOP_CONDITION (0)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Visual Studio with really aggressive warnings enabled needs this to avoid compiler complaints\[char46]
.PP
the
.BR "do {} while (0);"
trick is useful for wrapping code in a macro that may or may not be a single statement, to avoid various C language accidents\[char46]
.PP
To use:

.IP
.EX
do { SomethingOnce(); } while (SDL_NULL_WHILE_LOOP_CONDITION (0));
.EE
.PP

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

